From: qian <ruiqian.tang@seeed.cc>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: add Awinic AW21009/AW2023 face board LED drivers
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [hardware-specific]

Face Board V1.0 (sch_261020) replaces the PCA9535 + NPN LED circuitry with
two constant-current drivers: an AW21009 (9 channels, I2C 0x20) for the
indicator LEDs and an AW2023 (3 channels, 0x45) for the RGB LED.

leds-aw210xx.c is Awinic's vendor driver (one "aw21009" classdev with
singleled/effect/rgbcolor sysfs), carried here with board-verified fixes:

- AW21009_GROUP_ENABLE 0x38 -> 0x07: 0x38 sets only GCFG reserved bits and
  enables no group, so group mode never took effect (GROUP_DISABLE stays
  0x40: GSLDIS=1 keeps per-LED SL color, 0x00 leaves LEDs dark on hardware).
- APSE disabled at probe: with it on, the chip enters power-save after 32ms
  with all LEDs off and then ignores SL/BR updates for seconds.
- probe fails when the LED classdev registration fails, enable-gpio is
  optional (EN is pulled up on board), and an OF modalias alias allows
  module autoloading.

leds-aw2023.c is a minimal manual-mode driver (one classdev per channel,
brightness = PWM duty).

diff --git a/drivers/leds/Kconfig b/drivers/leds/Kconfig
index b9262d1da1ee..567d7091989e 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/leds/Kconfig
@@ -105,6 +105,26 @@ config LEDS_AW2013
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
 	  will be called leds-aw2013.
 
+config LEDS_AW2023
+	tristate "LED support for Awinic AW2023"
+	depends on LEDS_CLASS && I2C && OF
+	help
+	  This option enables support for the AW2023 3-channel
+	  LED driver.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
+	  will be called leds-aw2023.
+
+config LEDS_AW210XX
+	tristate "LED support for Awinic AW21009/12/18"
+	depends on LEDS_CLASS && I2C
+	help
+	  This option enables support for the AW210XX family multi-channel
+	  LED driver (vendor port from Awinic).
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
+	  will be called leds-aw210xx.
+
 config LEDS_BCM6328
 	tristate "LED Support for Broadcom BCM6328"
 	depends on LEDS_CLASS
